<title>MOROCCO: Morocco to turn hotel into hospital.</title>
<headline>Morocco to turn hotel into hospital.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan parliament has pulled a three-star state hotel off the list for privatisation to enable it to be turned into a hospital.</p>
<p>The official Moroccan news agency MAP said on Tuesday parliament amended the law so that Al Massira hotel, in Oujda on the Moroccan-Algerian frontier, could fill a local need for medical facilities.</p>
<p>Morocco has so far sold 18 of 37 hotels originally on the list for privatisation by the end of 1998, along with 77 firms.</p>
<p>The privatisation ministry is waiting for offers on nine hotels advertised for sale in November at a minimum total price of $11 million. Closing date is January 10.</p>
</text>
